900 MB / 28.0 ms = ~32 GB/s, which IS a plausible roof. So the kernel is
memory-bound exactly as you say, but it is bound on **8.8x the bytes an INT8
kernel moves** -- and INT8 is precisely what the NPU runs and what S12 validated.

