~21% of corpus, which may be a corpus-statistics floor nobody beats by
shaping. That measurement costs one run and nobody has done it.

### The question that decides whether any of it is a network

FINAL_REPORT names it as the biggest risk and it is still open: **who
pays for the second run.** Verification measured as approximately full
re-execution — 85 ms recompute against 0.7 ms of commitment checking. And
`hyperjob_v0.proto` still lacks the commit/reveal worker-bound seal, so
replication as currently specified is theatre: replica two echoes replica
one's hash and manufactures agreement.

That is the layer that killed the predecessors. BOINC: twenty years, no
market. Golem: built one, repo deleted. Akash: real market, rents VMs and
not phones.

### Methodological warning that applies to all of the above

Every constant in S5/S11/S17 was chosen on a self-authored synthetic
uniform graph. AGENT-3's rule, which I am adopting: *a self-authored case
may catch a regression but must never choose a value.* The one
