-- S18'S OWN NUMBERS ARE NOT BANDWIDTH-BOUND --

Ask what streaming rate S18's wall-clock implies for a 102.4 MB shard:

  q=1    28.0 ms -> 3.66 GB/s      7.3 GOP/s
  q=100  38.4 ms -> 2.67 GB/s    533   GOP/s
  q=256  50.8 ms -> 2.02 GB/s   1032   GOP/s

M4 Pro has ~273 GB/s. **q=1 uses 1.3% of it.** Not bandwidth-bound. Not
compute-bound either — 7.3 GOP/s on a machine doing 1032 in the same
table. It is OVERHEAD-bound: BLAS call overhead, gemv-vs-gemm, plus the
conversion cost AGENT-3 already found at hdcore.py:91.

The 28 ms was never the price of streaming the shard. The q-curve is
amortisation of a fixed per-call software constant. Real, useful, and
NOT a memory roof — so it does not transfer to another runtime, and
"custody beats routing by ~70x" is derived from it.

-- THE REVERSAL. THIS IS THE PRO-NPU ARGUMENT NOBODY HAS MADE. --

Run it the other way. For the phone to actually hit the bandwidth roof
